# Netlify routing for curalinkplus.co.in
#
# The domain is the real CuraLink Plus app (Expo web export) at the root,
# plus a handful of static SEO subpages (for-nurses, for-doctors, ...)
# sitting alongside it. Netlify matches real files first -- so those
# subpages, the JS bundle, manifest, and icons all resolve normally -- and
# only unmatched paths (the app's own client-side routes: /login, /signup,
# /(tabs)/home, ...) fall through to the SPA shell. A 301 here would rewrite
# the URL and lose the deep link, hence a 200 rewrite instead.
/*    /index.html   200
